    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-321728",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Non-Special Angles",
      "problem": "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ Round your answers to **the nearest integer**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2 & =0 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-2 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-0.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-0.4)=-21.8014{…}^{∘}≈-{22.80}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince $-{22.80}^{∘}$ lies outside the domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate solutions in the domain, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={180}^{∘}+(-{21.80}^{∘})≈{158.20}^{∘},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={360}^{∘}+(-{21.80}^{∘})≈{338.20}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are $x={158}^{∘}$ and $x={338}^{∘}.$",
      "answer_fields": [
